# Title: Access To Crypto Currency Wallets By Uncommon Applications
# ID: f41b0311-44f9-44f0-816d-dd45e39d4bc8
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2024-07-29
# Tags: attack.t1003, attack.credential-access
# Description: Detects file access requests to crypto currency files by uncommon processes.
# Could indicate potential attempt of crypto currency wallet stealing.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\Ethereum\\keystore\\* OR FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\EthereumClassic\\keystore\\* OR FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\monero\\wallets\\*)) OR ((FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\Bitcoin\\wallet.dat OR FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\BitcoinABC\\wallet.dat OR FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\BitcoinSV\\wallet.dat OR FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\DashCore\\wallet.dat OR FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\DogeCoin\\wallet.dat OR FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\Litecoin\\wallet.dat OR FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\Ripple\\wallet.dat OR FileName:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\Zcash\\wallet.dat))) AND -((((process_name:C:\\Program Files (x86)\\* OR process_name:C:\\Program Files\\* OR process_name:C:\\Windows\\system32\\* OR process_name:C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\*)) OR (process_name:"System"))) AND -((process_name:C:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\* AND (process_name:*\\MpCopyAccelerator.exe OR process_name:*\\MsMpEng.exe))))
